From 5c7b9a1e915b844bbf6c06813a849563daa268bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Hotchkiss <chris@hotchkiss.io>
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 16:34:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] P1: drive the emulated Skylander portal over an AF_UNIX
 IPC socket

Adds a self-contained IPC listener to the emulated Skylander USB device so an
external controller (skylander-portal-controller) can load/clear figures and
read emulator state without touching the Skylanders Manager GUI dialog.

- Skylander.h: 3 read-only slot accessors on sky_portal
  (first_free_slot / slot_loaded / slot_serial).
- Skylander.cpp: an AF_UNIX SOCK_STREAM listener started once from the
  usb_device_skylander ctor (mirrors the AF_UNIX server already in Emu/GDB.cpp).
  Commands: PING / STATE / WINDOW / STATUS / LOAD <path.sky> / CLEAR <slot>,
  plus a 1 Hz heartbeat push (Emu.GetStatus + g_progr_* boot/shader-compile
  progress + RSX int_flip_index frame counter). LOAD/CLEAR call the same
  g_skyportal API the GUI uses. Socket path via $SKYLANDER_IPC_PATH.
  WinSock2 headers are included before any transitive <windows.h> (RSXThread.h)
  to avoid winsock v1/v2 redefinition clashes.
- Defines g_game_window_handle here in emucore; P2 (gs_frame) publishes into it.

Shallow + additive; no new .cpp / no rpcs3.vcxproj entry. PLAN 16.1.2 / 16.3.x.
